Rembric OpenCode V2 plugin (`extensions/rembric/`)
===================================================

This is the local `extensions/rembric/` package: an OpenCode V2 plugin loaded
by OpenCode from its plugin directory. It is not an OpenChamber guest
extension, does not appear in OpenChamber's extension list, and OpenChamber's
service approval does not apply to it.

core/rembric-plugin-core.mjs and core/rembric-dotenv.mjs are vendored
unmodified from the Rembric project:

  https://github.com/susomejias/rembric
  apps/plugin/bin/rembric-plugin-core.mjs
  apps/plugin/mcp-bridge/rembric-dotenv.mjs

Rembric is MIT licensed. Copyright its authors. Copyright (c) 2026 Rembric
contributors. The vendored files carry no local modifications; the V2 adapter
in index.ts is independently written against OpenCode's documented V2 plugin
API.

The default export is a plain `{ id, setup }` object, so the built bundle
inlines both vendored files and has no runtime dependencies.

The full MIT permission notice for the vendored Rembric code is reproduced in
[`THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES`](THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES), because the bundle strips
comments and therefore cannot carry the notice in a header.
